<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka's benchmark 12-month T-bills edge up.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka's benchmark 12-month T-bills edge up.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yields of 12-month and three-month treasury bills moved up by 0.04 and 0.05 percentage points respectively at Wednesday's auction, while six-month bills eased by 0.08 points, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		   Bids received   Bids accepted   Avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     1,216	     1,206	  10.54 (10.49)</p>
<p>    6 months     1,346		 625	  11.54 (11.62)</p>
<p>    12 months	715		 645	  12.74 (12.70)</p>
<p>    Total	  3,277	     2,476</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets).</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
